A||||7||DJRice||Cold Start Switch
Z||000000||DJRice||08-19-99||02:01 PM||||My 87 V6 auto now requires some warm up time.<br>When I start it in the morning the RPMs will rise to 1000+ and then drop to 500 and then go back to 1000 or more then back to 500.  <br>After cylcing like this for a minute, everything runs like a top.  Is this the sign of a bad cold start switch?  Where is this cold start switch?
Z||000001||Formula||08-19-99||04:39 PM||||Mine does that to. 
Z||000002||mwbackus||08-19-99||06:07 PM||||No, the cold start switch only activates for an instant upon starting.  The IAC valve is responsible for idle mixture after the engine is running.  This flucuation in idle  can be indicative of a vacuum leak, or to be more precise, the IAC is unable to adjust quickly enough to compensate for the additional airflow and fluxuations caused by the vacuum leak.  Any other condition where the IAC is hindered from proper adjustment can also cause this, so it is advisable to remove it and clean the pintle and seat.  The IAC is an intregral part of the FI system.  Since it is both an electical and mechanical part(stepper motor), it tends to wear/malfunction frequently.  Although they are expensive, it is an item that I replace if there is any question as to its age or condition. <p>Mike
Z||000003||Speadraser||08-20-99||05:23 AM||||If you decide to clean it be carefull with the IAC the pintle does not move freely or slide back and forth, it has a screw action.  I've read of other readers trying to adjust  the pintle thinking it was frozen in one position and ended up breaking it.  There is a pintle reseting procedure I have read about in one of my manuals I'll look it up and post it here next week.<br>Speady
Z||000004||DJRice||08-20-99||07:22 AM||||How much does one of these gadgets cost?
Z||000005||Linx||08-20-99||08:52 AM||||$25 at an Autozone.<br>There are two kinds of IAC's.  One can be set by pushing in the pintle, the other one by turning it.  I've read you can determine your type by looking at the "collar".  The new IAC will have instructions with it.
Z||000006||K9||09-01-99||11:18 PM||||I have the same problem with my 85 Gt. What is an IAC.If possible can anyone put the above answers in english.<br>
Z||000007||lowCG||09-01-99||11:29 PM||||Lots of little things can cause these symptoms;weak spark,timing off a little,bad gas,vacume loss,old plugs,wrong heat range/low quality plugs,or wires even.I'd check all the ignition possibilities before I went and changed the IAC valve,or it's settings(twist,or shove).
